{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nCompaction preserves folded event sources as `*.retired` (invariant I1, epic b306); retention is permanent, so tombstones — and the whole per-event commit/tree history — accumulate on the `tickets` branch. This blocks health-lane bug `defensive-buckskin-rhino` (`a453-193b-2864-451b`): the blobless CI checkout pack is ~481 MiB vs a deliberate 100 MiB budget (`verify-identity.yml:47`). A `git gc`/repack does NOT shrink it (proven). The only lever is reducing reachable commit/tree objects on `tickets` history — causally-safe history reclamation, which requires the causal-stability proof this epic owns.\n\n## Operator decision (2026-08-24, in comments)\nStability model = **option 2 (remote-anchored horizon) + stale-clone forced override**, N=30d default; residual loss of a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent work is ACCEPTED.\n\n## Design + proof (full detail in the DESIGN + PROOF comment)\nCausal-stability boundary C1–C5: an event is reclaimable iff (C1) folded by a committed SNAPSHOT, (C2) that fold reachable on the sync remote's `tickets` ref ≥ N days, (C3) stale clones (> N days) forced to reset to remote (no reintroduction), (C4) its signature is carried in the SNAPSHOT `authorship_ledger` OR `identity.enforce_since` is re-anchored to grandfather it, (C5) no unfolded state depends on it (I9). Under C1–C5 no still-observable state changes, no signature verification breaks, no resurrection is possible.\n\nMeasured (origin/tickets): 235,482 commits, 408,295 trees, ZERO blobs blobless; trees ≈95% of bytes; root tree 270 KB × 6,008 flat ticket dirs re-emitted per commit; ~69% of commits are derived enrichment/digest churn; ~14K commits/day.\n\n## Quantified win — insufficient alone\n`.retired` files are blobs; the guarded pack is blobless ⇒ `.retired` GC alone shrinks it by ~0. The real lever is collapsing per-event history into SNAPSHOT-anchored checkpoints below the horizon. Max safe win at N=30d ≈ 365–380 MiB; N=7d ≈ 200–215 MiB; reaching ≤100 MiB needs an unsafe <4-day horizon. **So a temporary budget-raise bridge (W3) is unavoidable**, paired with structural fixes (out of scope, `discovered_from` this epic): W1 batch the enrichment/digest write lane; W2 shard the flat ticket dirs to shrink root-tree churn.\n\n## Mechanism (portable, out-of-band; NO CI-provider dependence)\nOffline reclamation in a disposable clone (I9b isolation), never on an interactive path or under the store lock:\n- **S1** remote-anchored eligibility (horizon computation) — pure git reachability + timestamps.\n- **S2** history coalescing to a re-signed baseline checkpoint = compacted as-of-horizon state + carried authorship_ledger; re-anchor `identity.enforce_since` to the baseline. Broadened from `.retired`-only to commit/tree reclamation (the object-count lever).\n- **S3** stale-clone detection + forced remote-override on reconnect.\n- **S0** ADR: amend §I1 permanent-retention doctrine; prove I1–I9 hold under the horizon with the accepted >N-day loss.\n\n## Risk / rollback\nA rewrite changes every commit SHA ⇒ every clone/worktree diverges (non-FF force-update of a shared, auto-pushed, high-write-rate branch); live clones with unpushed writes need a write-fence/maintenance window. Rollback: immutable backup ref `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-<date>` before the swap; stage on a shadow branch verified by `rebar fsck` + full-log replay + `verify-authorship`; the swap is one revertible ref update; never prune the backup until a green Verify Authorship Identity run + full reconcile.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] S0 ADR merged: §I1 doctrine amended; I1–I9 proven under the remote-anchored horizon + override; accepted >N-day loss stated.\n- [ ] S1 eligibility check: only SNAPSHOT-folded events whose fold is remote-reachable ≥ N days are eligible; recent ones excluded; portable (no single CI provider).\n- [ ] S2 coalescing prototyped on a DISPOSABLE SHADOW CLONE (I9b isolation, never pushed to origin/tickets): reachable commit/tree count reduced vs baseline; re-signed baseline; `enforce_since` re-anchored; `rebar fsck` + replay + `verify-authorship` clean ON THE SHADOW BRANCH; two-clone test shows a not-yet-observed fold is NOT reclaimed. No origin/tickets rewrite/force-push performed.\n- [ ] S3 stale-clone override enforced on reconnect.\n- [ ] docs/concurrency.md §I1 updated from 'follow-up' to 'implemented'.\n- [ ] Health-lane note: quantify residual pack size; confirm the W3 budget bridge value + W1/W2 follow-ups filed.\n\n## HARD STOP (this design slice only)\nThis slice is DESIGN + PROOF only: no history rewrite / force-push / destructive reclaim executed, and none of the S0–S3 acceptance criteria above are implemented here. The S2 shadow-clone prototype and every other S0–S3 implementation happen in later child slices AFTER human approval, and never mutate origin/tickets or the Gerrit box until the approved staged rollout. Escalated to the orchestrator for human approval before any destructive action."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788035869651357798,"uuid":"f04db02f-fb70-406d-b1bb-b3f5fdd319c0"}